# Boot battery guard, drained latch: the low-battery shutdown is only a
# backup and never writes under disk-safe. The sim boots at 3,450 mV with
# a clear record; 3 s after power-on the cell reads 1,000 mV
# (IPODUI_SIM_DRAIN_AT_MS), so the filter falls through the 0 % window
# (3,300 to the sim's disk-safe 3,200) in about 3 s, inside the 0 %
# write's 30 s wait for an awake disk, and query_force_shutdown() fires
# under disk-safe: clean_shutdown() skips the latch. (On the unit the
# fall through the window takes minutes; a fall this fast is a cut.)
#   SIM_BUILD=build/sim-ui scripts/shots.sh tests/ui/ipodui-p16-bootbatt-latch-shutdown.script
# env: IPODUI_SIM_BATT_MV=3450
# env: IPODUI_SIM_DRAINED=0
# env: IPODUI_SIM_DRAIN_AT_MS=3000
# golden: skip
# log: bootbatt latch drained=0 boot mv=3450
# log: bootbatt latch shutdown skipped latched=0
# log: sys lowbatt empty=1
# nolog: bootbatt latch set
# nolog: sys deadbatt
# nolog: splash-pass

wait 4000
shot main_menu
wait 40000
shot never_reached       # the low-battery shutdown exited the sim
